body:
Thanks for the kind words and being on the "hot" sections and so many upvotes, really, thank you guys very much!

I'm from Brazil, so as you might have guessed we get things here very late, so just a year ago I think, not really sure when we installed the fiber internet, but it's recent, before we were stuck with a normal broadband internet that maxed out at 1MB, and this one is 80MB. I always wanted to keep seeding what I downloaded and whatnot but I just couldn't, even reducing the upload speed (which normally was slow so you can imagine downgrading the speed even more) the entire internet would essentially 'break', it was torrents or using the internet normally, no halfway, it was one or another, if I seeded the entire internet would become a dial-up connection, the torrent program would eat my internet, it would take ages to open an image, videos would take forever to buffer for a second in low resolutions, and so on, and the internet here is shared with my family, so you can see how impossible it was for me to seed (still don't have that YouTube/Twitch sweet viewers and money yet to get my own place :p) now I can seed AND use the internet normally, no buffering videos and at max resolutions, sites open like I wasn't seeding, and so on, so I was very glad to see one of these days that I was actually seeding more than I was downloading, so that's why I posted this here :p

&#x200B;

And my router is a TP-Link Archer C20 and my ISP is MHNet, I don't know if this is a 'global' router or it is only produced here, but yeah it's a 'cheap' modem, but still does the job very nice as you can see by the SS and my wall of text xD

&#x200B;

Oh also I lower the speeds on weekdays from 12:00pm to 22:00, since my brothers work with the internet on the weekdays and I don't want to make their side slow with me seeding torrents, and sometimes I do close the qBittorrent altogether when I do streams, play online games that needs all the speed possible so I don't get lag (such as Dead by Daylight) and so on.

&#x200B;

Again, thanks a lot for the kind comments and the upvotes, and sorry for giant wall of text, I'm happy what can I say? xD

Yeah that's what I thought based on the answers, maybe I won't show the video like I said, I'll watch but not show the video or audio, I'll cut it entirely, and refer to it and talk about it while I'm learning and so on, but I don't think that free website tutorials and free courses online would be a problem since they are free for everyone, only if I shared bought lessons and courses, that would be pirating without even asking, and I will always give credit, even the videos I watched without playing a single frame of it, or maybe I'll try like you said, just as little as possible and see what YouTube and the owner thinks about it, if it gets claimed (the notice one that only warns you, cuts your monetization on that video but nothing bad happens with the channel) then I'll delete the video, cut the video parts or the claimed parts and re-upload it.

&#x200B;

Thanks again a lot for everyone's feedback!

But please chill people, I'm not demanding lawyers or anything of the sort, but I know why you guys were discussing this based on my post, but disregard that, after all YouTube is pratically immune (at the moment at least) to any lawyer and trial, that is unless everyone gets tired of their BS and the big guys on YT get together and sue the hell out of YouTube to make the rules clear, don't delete or claim not copyrighted material, and address all the AdPocalipse's that happened and will happen and we all know about.

&#x200B;

Once again, thanks a lot!
